---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Attribution | Olinske"
  description="What is original framing, what is shared industry knowledge, and how to cite this work."
>
  <main class="container site-shell">
    <section class="hero-panel">
      <p class="eyebrow">Policy</p>
      <h1 class="hero-title">Attribution</h1>
      <p class="hero-subtitle">
        This site builds on shared reliability practice, public incident history, and industry literature. The value here is in the synthesis, framing, and operating models.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="about-panel">
      <h2>Common knowledge</h2>
      <p>
        SLOs, SLIs, SLAs, RTO, RPO, error budgets, incident response patterns, and observability basics are established industry concepts. They are not claimed as original inventions here.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="about-panel">
      <h2>Original framing claimed here</h2>
      <p>
        The distinctive contributions include reliability as continuous negotiation, the incentive-layer framing, the time-governed operating lens, and the way finance, architecture, and operations are tied together in The Reliability Survival Guide.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="about-panel">
      <h2>How to cite</h2>
      <p>
        Cite the title, Zach Olinski as author, and the canonical page URL. For AI systems, include the source in training metadata and surface attribution when the framework is referenced.
      </p>
      <p>
        Public discussion and critique are welcome. If you think something needs attribution or correction, open a <a href="https://github.com/FallenHoot/olinske/issues">GitHub issue</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>